# CyberTirah Framework Project Structure

This is a PHP-based MVC framework with a unique modular architecture. Understanding the project structure is essential for development.

## Core Architecture

The framework follows a "Body-Brain" architecture:
- **Brain**: Core framework classes and utilities ([Brain/](mdc:Brain/))
- **Body**: Application modules and business logic ([Body/](mdc:Body/))
- **Index**: Entry point and routing ([Index/](mdc:Index/))

## Key Directories

### Core Framework
- [Brain/ct_brain.php](mdc:Brain/ct_brain.php) - Main framework bootstrap and initialization
- [Brain/Core/](mdc:Brain/Core/) - Core classes (Router, Registry, Controller, Model)
- [Brain/Classes/](mdc:Brain/Classes/) - Framework utility classes organized by functionality

### Application Modules
- [Body/admin/](mdc:Body/admin/) - Admin panel modules
- [Body/public/](mdc:Body/public/) - Public-facing modules
- [Body/api/](mdc:Body/api/) - API endpoints
- [Body/ai/](mdc:Body/ai/) - AI-related modules

### Module Structure
Each module follows MVC pattern:
```
ModuleName/
├── routes.json          # Route definitions
├── Controllers/         # Controller classes
├── Models/             # Model classes
└── Views/              # View templates (.ct files)
```

### Infrastructure & Services
- [Services/](mdc:Services/) - Microservices (frontend, node-api, python-api, php-app)
- [Infra/](mdc:Infra/) - Docker and deployment configurations
- [Storage/](mdc:Storage/) - Static assets, cache, logs, uploads

### Shared Resources
- [Shared/](mdc:Shared/) - Shared data models, documentation, utilities
- [Tests/](mdc:Tests/) - Test suites

## Entry Points
- [Index/index.php](mdc:Index/index.php) - Main application entry point
- [frame_structure.json](mdc:frame_structure.json) - Project structure definition
- [installed.lock](mdc:installed.lock) - Installation status indicator

## Key Framework Files
- [Brain/ct_brain.php](mdc:Brain/ct_brain.php) - Bootstrap class with environment loading
- [Brain/Core/Router.php](mdc:Brain/Core/Router.php) - Routing system
- [Brain/Core/Registry.php](mdc:Brain/Core/Registry.php) - Dependency injection container

## Development Guidelines
- Always follow the MVC pattern for new modules
- Use the Registry for dependency injection
- Place new classes in appropriate Brain/Classes subdirectories
- Follow the established naming conventions
- Use .ct files for view templates
- Configure routes in routes.json files